.TH pepe-serve 1  pepe "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pepe\-serve \- Serve pepe over HTTP: start, watch, steer and compare runs from a script, an agent or a browser; loopback and a token by default
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpepe serve\fR [\fB\-\-listen\fR] [\fB\-\-token\-file\fR] [\fB\-\-max\-runs\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Serve pepe over HTTP: start, watch, steer and compare runs from a script, an agent or a browser; loopback and a token by default
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-listen\fR \fI<ADDR>\fR
Where to listen: 127.0.0.1:7878 by default. Any address but loopback needs \-\-allow\-host and the \-\-max\-requests, \-\-max\-rate and \-\-max\-concurrency caps
.TP
\fB\-\-token\-file\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
The tokens that may call the API, a line each: `name token`, or the token alone. Without one, a token is made and printed
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-runs\fR \fI<N>\fR [default: 1]
Runs going at once, on this machine and the workers together
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
